---
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import '../../styles/sound-analyzer.css';
const title = 'Digital Workbench — Browser Tools | WorkshopGirl';
const description = 'The WorkshopGirl Digital Workbench: analyze sound, inspect engine and speaker observations, validate DSP, and manage workshop jobs, parts and billing locally in your browser.';
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" /><title>{title}</title><meta name="description" content={description} /><link rel="canonical" href="https://workshopgirl.com/tools/" /><meta property="og:title" content={title} /><meta property="og:description" content={description} /><meta property="og:type" content="website" /><meta property="og:url" content="https://workshopgirl.com/tools/" /><link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" /></head><body><SiteHeader current="tools" /><main><div class="hero"><span class="eyebrow">WorkshopGirl tools</span><h1>The digital <span>workbench.</span></h1><p>Practical tools for a closer look at the machines and sounds around you.</p></div>
  <section class="tool-category" id="diagnostics" aria-labelledby="diagnostics-heading"><h2 id="diagnostics-heading">Diagnostics</h2><div class="tool-grid">
    <a class="tool-card" href="/tools/sound-analyzer/"><span class="eyebrow">Audio / locally in your browser</span><h2>Sound Analyzer</h2><p>Live microphone or audio file. Waveform, frequency spectrum, spectrogram and a useful before/after comparison.</p><strong>Open Sound Analyzer →</strong></a>
    <a class="tool-card" href="/tools/engine-sound-analyzer/"><span class="eyebrow">Engine sound / Live measurement</span><h2>Engine Sound Analyzer</h2><p>Inspect harmonics and persistent peaks with optional RPM and firing references. Capture before/after snapshots while live, without recording.</p><strong>Open Engine Sound Analyzer →</strong></a>
    <a class="tool-card" href="/tools/speaker-sound-analyzer/"><span class="eyebrow">Music / Captured frequency balance</span><h2>Speaker Sound Analyzer</h2><p>Play music. See its frequency balance. Explore bass, mid and treble with a simple captured sound profile.</p><strong>Open Speaker Sound Analyzer →</strong></a>
    <a class="tool-card" href="/tools/dsp-validation/"><span class="eyebrow">Audio / Validation utility</span><h2>DSP Validation Workbench</h2><p>Inspect and validate the digital signal processing pipeline with known signals and repeatable checks.</p><strong>Open DSP Validation →</strong></a>
  </div></section>
  <section class="tool-category workshop-category" id="workshop-operations" aria-labelledby="operations-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Private local workshop workflow</p><h2 id="operations-heading">Workshop Operations</h2><p>Keep one job connected from vehicle arrival through inspection, repair and handover. Records are stored in this browser.</p><div class="tool-grid">
    <a class="tool-card" href="/tools/workshop/vehicle-intake/"><span class="eyebrow">Step 1 / Start a job</span><h3>Vehicle Intake</h3><p>Capture customer, vehicle, arrival and reported concerns.</p><strong>Open Vehicle Intake →</strong></a>
    <a class="tool-card" href="/tools/workshop/inspection-estimate/"><span class="eyebrow">Step 2 / Inspect and estimate</span><h3>Inspection &amp; Estimate</h3><p>Use vehicle checklists, findings and an itemized estimate.</p><strong>Open Inspection &amp; Estimate →</strong></a>
    <a class="tool-card" href="/tools/workshop/work-order/"><span class="eyebrow">Step 3 / Record repair</span><h3>Work Order</h3><p>Carry approved work into technician tasks, materials and notes.</p><strong>Open Work Order →</strong></a>
    <a class="tool-card" href="/tools/workshop/qc-handover/"><span class="eyebrow">Step 4 / Verify and return</span><h3>QC &amp; Handover</h3><p>Complete quality checks, road-test notes and customer handover.</p><strong>Open QC &amp; Handover →</strong></a>
    <a class="tool-card" href="/tools/workshop/queue/"><span class="eyebrow">Operational dashboard / Existing workshop jobs</span><h3>Queue / Job Status</h3><p>See every saved Workshop Job, its derived status and the next step in the same workflow.</p><strong>Open Workshop Queue →</strong></a>
    <a class="tool-card" href="/tools/workshop/parts-inventory/"><span class="eyebrow">Local inventory / Job-linked movements</span><h3>Parts Inventory</h3><p>Track stock from ledger movements and issue parts to existing Workshop Jobs.</p><strong>Open Parts Inventory →</strong></a>
    <a class="tool-card" href="/tools/workshop/service-history/"><span class="eyebrow">Completed work / Local vehicle records</span><h3>Service History &amp; Warranty</h3><p>Review completed service timelines, document explicit warranty coverage and claims, and record the next service recommendation.</p><strong>Open Service History →</strong></a>
    <a class="tool-card" href="/tools/workshop/billing/"><span class="eyebrow">Commercial workbench / Local invoices</span><h3>Billing</h3><p>Review actual charges, confirm selling prices, issue invoices, record payments and print receipts.</p><strong>Open Workshop Billing →</strong></a>
    <a class="tool-card" href="/tools/workshop/procurement/"><span class="eyebrow">Parts purchasing / Local supplier orders</span><h3>Procurement</h3><p>Confirm purchase needs, issue supplier orders, record partial receipts and post accepted stock through the inventory ledger.</p><strong>Open Workshop Procurement →</strong></a>
  </div></section><p>Build your understanding with our <a href="/tutorials/">workshop tutorials</a>.</p></main><SiteFooter /><style>.tool-category{margin:3rem auto;max-width:1100px;padding:0 1rem}.tool-category>h2{font-size:clamp(1.7rem,4vw,2.4rem);margin:.25rem 0 1rem}.tool-category>p:not(.eyebrow){max-width:60ch}.tool-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,250px),1fr));gap:1rem}.tool-card{display:block}.workshop-category{border-top:1px solid #ddd;padding-top:2rem}.tool-card h3{font-size:1.35rem}</style></body></html>
